            <ArticleTitle>'Negativicoccus massiliensis', a new species identified from human stool from an obese patient after bariatric surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.nmni.2016.05.018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report here the main characteristics of 'Negativicoccus massiliensis' strain AT7 (CSURP = P2082, DSM = 100853) isolated from a stool sample collected from a 47-year-old obese French man before bariatric surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
